  "slug": "mitochondrial-resource-16ed",
  "summary": "New leakage-controlled benchmarks, domain and membrane-protein resources, and diverse-population references target gaps in variant interpretation and pipeline validation.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is infrastructure for interpreting human genetic variation, with emphasis on rigorous evaluation and population coverage. For missense variants, a leakage-controlled benchmark yields a gradient-boosting consensus predictor, while MetaDome 2027 aggregates population and pathogenic evidence across homologous Pfam domains with GRCh38 support. memVar links ~10.9M ClinVar, COSMIC and gnomAD SNVs across 7,732 membrane proteins to topology and lipid contacts. A truth-based in silico framework tests clinical sequencing pipelines from simulated reads to reportable findings. Population-scale resources broaden context: a 490,319-genome UK Biobank haplotype panel improves imputation versus TOPMed r3, a Qatar Biobank catalog reports ~7M transcriptome QTLs, and a heritability study spans 198,931 diverse individuals. The items are heterogeneous; the shared advance is coupling scoring with structural context, validation and diverse cohorts.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-06"
}
